import{_ as o,o as a,c as n,a2 as t}from"./chunks/framework.C6DVv5ZP.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Working by area","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"docs/agents/areas.md","filePath":"docs/agents/areas.md"}'),i={name:"docs/agents/areas.md"};function s(r,e,d,c,l,h){return a(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t('<h1 id="working-by-area" tabindex="-1">Working by area <a class="header-anchor" href="#working-by-area" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Working by area&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Five areas of the repo used to have a long-running role thread each. They no longer do: the knowledge lives in the files below, and any short thread reads them before it works. Only the <strong>Maintainer</strong> stays a long-running thread, because it collects <code>// CLEANUP:</code> markers over time.</p><p>A task thread reads the section for each area it touches, does the work itself, and asks the owner (one decision, with a recommended option) when the docs don&#39;t settle it. There is one review per PR, not one per area.</p><h2 id="architect-model-engine-schema" tabindex="-1">Architect: model, engine, schema <a class="header-anchor" href="#architect-model-engine-schema" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Architect: model, engine, schema&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Read <code>CONTEXT.md</code>, <code>docs/adr/</code>, <code>docs/architecture.md</code>.</p><ul><li>Name things with the glossary&#39;s words. A word the glossary lacks is added to <code>CONTEXT.md</code> in the same PR.</li><li>A decision that would surprise the next reader gets an ADR in the same PR (next free number, then the sidebar picks it up). Say explicitly when a change contradicts one.</li><li>Before changing a stored shape (database, catalog, files on the phone), check whether existing installs break. If they do, ask the owner whether migration or backward-compatibility code is wanted, and write none until they answer. A schema change is a new SQLDelight migration.</li><li>Logic lives in shared Kotlin with a test. Apps and the server never decide what a workout is.</li><li>Domain text reaches Kotlin through typed generated functions (<code>DomainText</code>), not string lookups (<a href="./../adr/0014-text-lives-in-one-json-file-per-language-and-namespace">ADR 0014</a>). A generator that writes files also deletes the stale ones it wrote before.</li><li>A change in <code>build-logic</code> or the shared engine gets its tests run with <code>./gradlew jvmTest jsTest :server:test :tools:i18n:test</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="designer-screens-and-mockups" tabindex="-1">Designer: screens and mockups <a class="header-anchor" href="#designer-screens-and-mockups" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Designer: screens and mockups&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Read <a href="./../design-system">the design system</a> and <a href="./../adr/0016-mockups-are-plain-html-in-the-repo">ADR 0016</a>.</p><ul><li>A screen starts as an HTML mockup in <code>design/mockups/drafts/</code>. A separate, later PR moves it to <code>agreed/</code> once the owner has reviewed it on the docs site. Nothing is built from a draft, and a ticket with no agreed mockup waits for one.</li><li>Mockups use <code>var(--cp-*)</code> roles only, so one file works in light and dark. Check both on the docs site before opening the PR.</li><li>Android and iOS mirror each other. When they disagree, the agreed mockup wins; when the mockup is wrong, fix it in a PR rather than diverging in code.</li><li>Words never break: text is laid out for the longest language. A tab label has about 12 characters of room; shrink or shorten it before letting a word wrap.</li><li>The warm-up is headed by the builder&#39;s sun icon in every mockup and screen.</li><li>The English screen copy follows <code>docs/brand.md</code>; every string is also added in French (see Translator below).</li><li>Theme files are generated from <code>design/tokens.json</code>: edit the tokens, then run <code>node design/build-tokens.mjs</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="poulpy-keeper-the-mascot" tabindex="-1">Poulpy keeper: the mascot <a class="header-anchor" href="#poulpy-keeper-the-mascot" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Poulpy keeper: the mascot&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Read <a href="./../brand">the brand</a> and <a href="./../brand-decisions">the brand decisions</a>.</p><ul><li>Poulpy is never guilt. Pain or rehab always shows the blue side for 72 h; errors are crimson with an icon, never ember.</li><li>Skipping a planned session never counts as missing it; only entries left hanging do. Ember is a comic mood, not a penalty.</li><li>Poulpy speaks in short first-person lines, warm and a little cheeky. He says <em>tu</em> in French while the app says <em>vous</em>.</li><li>A new reward, notification, pose or reaction rule is written into <code>docs/brand.md</code> (and <code>docs/brand-decisions.md</code> when it settles an open question) in the same PR. At most one notification a day.</li><li>Drawings are generated: edit <code>design/build-poulpy.mjs</code>, then run <code>node design/build-poulpy.mjs</code>.</li><li>The body map figures are generated too: edit <code>design/build-body-map.mjs</code> or the outlines in <code>design/body-map-source/</code> (keep its NOTICE.md), then run <code>node design/build-body-map.mjs</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="translator-text-in-every-language" tabindex="-1">Translator: text in every language <a class="header-anchor" href="#translator-text-in-every-language" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Translator: text in every language&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Read <a href="./../../i18n/README"><code>i18n/README.md</code></a> and the glossaries in <code>i18n/glossary/</code>.</p><ul><li>A new or edited string goes into <code>i18n/messages/en</code> and <code>i18n/messages/fr</code> in the same PR. Never write a native string file; Android, iOS and <code>DomainText</code> are generated.</li><li>Counts must agree with their number: use an ICU plural for anything countable, so &quot;1 rep&quot; and « 1 tentacule » read right. Check the French forms (<code>one</code>, <code>many</code>, <code>other</code>) too.</li><li>French typography (non-breaking spaces before <code>: ; ? !</code> and inside « »), and the rest of the checks, are automated by <code>i18n/typography.mjs</code>.</li><li>Native speakers proofread in Fink, which opens pull requests. The docs page for them is &quot;Proofread and translate&quot; page of the Translations section; keep it free of repo paths.</li><li>Exercise text lives in <code>catalog.json</code>. Catalog slugs never change; retire an entry with <code>&quot;retired&quot;: true</code> and raise <code>version</code>.</li><li>Text that might not fit on a phone (tab labels, buttons, chips) is read in French on a device before the language is called done.</li></ul><h2 id="maintainer-housekeeping-long-running" tabindex="-1">Maintainer: housekeeping (long-running) <a class="header-anchor" href="#maintainer-housekeeping-long-running" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Maintainer: housekeeping (long-running)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Maintainer owns <code>// CLEANUP:</code> markers, CI (<code>.github/workflows/</code>), <code>gradle/libs.versions.toml</code>, <code>.github/labels.yml</code>, the <code>device-test</code> checklists and triage.</p><ul><li>A change that leaves a workaround, shim, stopgap or known gap marks it <code>// CLEANUP:</code> with what to remove or fix and why, plus an issue number when there is one, and says so in the PR description.</li><li>Android and iOS only build in CI, so a PR is done when CI is green. Anything about Bluetooth, sound, haptics, background running or installs needs the <code>device-test</code> label and a line on what to check on a phone.</li></ul><h2 id="reviews" tabindex="-1">Reviews <a class="header-anchor" href="#reviews" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Reviews&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Each PR gets a single review, not one per area. The docs site workflow comments the preview and the pages to review; nobody posts a docs-review comment of their own. Put what the reviewer must know in the PR description.</p><h2 id="docs-on-the-site" tabindex="-1">Docs on the site <a class="header-anchor" href="#docs-on-the-site" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Docs on the site&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Every guideline, glossary entry, rule or decision is reachable from the published docs site in the PR that writes it: add the file to <code>site/published.mjs</code> and a sidebar entry in <code>site/.vitepress/config.mts</code>. CI fails otherwise.</p>',22)])])}const p=o(i,[["render",s]]);export{u as __pageData,p as default};
